2.176.2 emacsvox-ocr Options
----------------------------

 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-compress-image
     Command used to compress the scanned tiff file.

     Default Value:

     nil


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-compress-image-options
     Options used for compressing tiff image.

     Default Value:

     "-c g3 "


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-compress-photo-options
     Options used when created JPEG from  scanned photographs.

     Default Value:

     "-optimize -progressive"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-engine
     OCR engine used to process an image or PDF.

     Default Value:

     "<emacsvox-root>/bin/emacsvox-paddleocr"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-engine-options
     Additional command-line arguments passed literally to the OCR engine.
     For the bundled PaddleOCR adapter, these follow the typed customization
     options and can override them.

     Default Value:

     nil


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-error-buffer
     Buffer that receives diagnostics from the OCR engine.

     Default Value:

     "*Emacsvox OCR Errors*"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-image-extension
     Filename extension used for acquired image.

     Default Value:

     ".tif"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-jpeg-metadata-writer
     Program to add metadata to JPEG files.

     Default Value:

     "wrjpgcom"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-keep-uncompressed-image
     If set to T, uncompressed image is not removed.

     Default Value:

     nil


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-device
     Paddle device used by the bundled adapter.
     Examples include ‘cpu’, ‘gpu’, and ‘gpu:0’.

     Default Value:

     "cpu"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-enable-mkldnn
     Whether to enable oneDNN/MKL-DNN acceleration for PaddleOCR.
     Keep this disabled for the tested PaddlePaddle 3.3.0 CPU setup on WSL.

     Default Value:

     nil


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-language
     Language used by the bundled PaddleOCR adapter.

     Default Value:

     "en"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-python
     Python executable used by the bundled PaddleOCR adapter.
     When nil, the launcher uses its default isolated environment.  This option has
     no effect when ‘emacsvox-ocr-engine’ selects another OCR engine.

     Default Value:

     nil


 -- Variable: User Option
          emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-use-document-orientation
     Whether PaddleOCR should classify document orientation.

     Default Value:

     t


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-use-document-unwarping
     Whether PaddleOCR should correct warped document images.

     Default Value:

     t


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-use-formula-recognition
     Whether PaddleOCR should recognize mathematical formulas.

     Default Value:

     t


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-use-table-recognition
     Whether PaddleOCR should recognize and preserve tables.

     Default Value:

     t


 -- Variable: User Option
          emacsvox-ocr-paddleocr-use-text-line-orientation
     Whether PaddleOCR should classify individual text-line orientation.

     Default Value:

     t


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-photo-compress
     Program to create JPEG compressed images.

     Default Value:

     "cjpeg"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-scan-image-options
     Command line options to pass to image acquisition program.

     Default Value:

     "--resolution 300 --mode lineart --format=tiff"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-scan-photo-options
     Options  used when scanning in photographs.

     Default Value:

     "--mode color --format=pnm"


 -- Variable: User Option emacsvox-ocr-working-directory
     Directory where images and OCR results
     will be placed.

     Default Value:

     "~/.emacsvox/ocr/"



