2.207 emacsvox-setup
====================

Entry point for Emacsvox.  The simplest and most basic way to start
emacsvox is: emacs -q -l <emacsvox-dir>/lisp/emacsvox-setup.el The above
starts a vanilla Emacs with just Emacsvox loaded.  Loading this source
file also detects newer startup sources that would otherwise be hidden
by stale byte-code and temporarily prefers those sources.  Rebuild a
changed checkout rather than relying on that fallback.  Once the above
has been verified to work, You can add (load-library "emacsvox-setup")
To your .emacs file when using an installed, already-built copy.  See
tvr/emacs-startup.el in the Emacsvox Git repository for my setup.


File: emacsvox-reference.info,  Node: emacsvox-sgml-mode,  Next: emacsvox-sh-script,  Prev: emacsvox-setup,  Up: Emacsvox Commands And Options

